    "result_text": "Patronage is now mutual: if one person is another's patron, each counts as the other's patron, and a pair linked both ways counts once. `bin/e2e` passes, including the stored test-data check that runs before it.\n\nHow it works:\n- **Stored data is unchanged.** Patron links are saved exactly as given. When the people list is built, the server merges each person's own patrons with the people who name them as a patron, without duplicates. The new `PersonView.mutualPatrons` does this, and `PeopleService.list` calls it. Because nothing extra is stored, seeding and reading back the test data still return the rows as they were sent.\n- **Backing** adds up the momentum of every patron in that merged set. In the test, Ada names Ben and Cam, so Ben's and Cam's backing are now 18 each (Ada's momentum) instead of 0.\n- **The Patrons column** uses the same merged set, so Ben's row now lists Ada.\n- A person who names themselves as their own patron is ignored.\n\nThe only front-end edit is the comment on `backing` in `people.service.ts`, updated to say patronage is mutual. The Java doc comment on `PersonView` got the same update.",
